.TH JS8CALL\-MAP 1 "2026" "js8call-map" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
js8call-map \- live Maidenhead grid map of stations heard by JS8CALL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B js8call-map
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B js8call-map
connects to the TCP API of a running JS8CALL and shows the stations it hears
on an offline map in your web browser: signal reports, message history, who is
hearing you, day/night and greyline overlays, and distance and bearing tools.
.PP
The JS8Stat view decodes status reports (StatReps), incidents, group
alerts and group messages heard by JS8CALL in the formats used by
CommStat-compatible stations, shows them in tables and on the map,
and keeps them for a number of days. Optionally it can transmit these through
JS8CALL; the operator switches transmitting on in the map and confirms every
transmission. JS8Stat is part of js8call-map; it is not CommStat, not a new
version of CommStat, and not affiliated with the CommStat project.
.PP
In JS8CALL, enable the TCP server (File > Settings > Reporting, port 2237) and
set Max TCP Connections to 3.
.PP
By default the map is served at http://localhost:8181/ and opened in your
browser when a desktop session is available. With no desktop (an SSH login, a
headless Raspberry Pi or a systemd service) no browser is opened; browse to the
address it prints instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " addr"
Web interface address (default 127.0.0.1). Use 0.0.0.0 to reach the map from
other devices on your network.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
Web interface port (default 8181).
.TP
.BI \-\-js8\-host " addr"
JS8CALL TCP API host (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BI \-\-js8\-port " n"
JS8CALL TCP API port (default 2237).
.TP
.BI \-\-poll\-seconds " n"
How often to poll JS8CALL for activity (default 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl\-minutes " n"
Remove stations not heard for this long (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-messages " n"
Messages kept per station (default 100).
.TP
.BR \-\-open ", " \-\-no\-open
Open, or don't open, the map in your web browser at startup. On by default for
the installed program when a desktop is available.
.TP
.BI \-\-transmit " mode"
Who may send JS8Stat reports, alerts and messages through JS8CALL:
.B off
(never),
.B local
(default; only a browser on the same computer) or
.B lan
(any device that can open the map). Transmitting must also be switched on in
the map, and every transmission is confirmed by the operator.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " folder"
Where JS8Stat records are saved (default
.IR ~/.local/share/js8call\-map ).
.TP
.BI \-\-keep\-days " n"
Keep JS8Stat records for this many days (default 7).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read settings from this file instead of the usual locations.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " file"
Save the raw JS8CALL traffic to
.I file
(JSON Lines) for testing and troubleshooting. Stops at 100 MB.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/js8call\-map/config.json
System-wide settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/js8call\-map/config.json
Per-user settings; these override the system-wide file. For example:
.RS
.EX
{ "webHost": "0.0.0.0", "webPort": 8181 }
.EE
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/js8call\-map/js8stat.jsonl
Saved JS8Stat records (status reports, incidents, alerts and messages).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/js8call\-map.service
systemd user service for running the map without a desktop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each option can also be set with an environment variable:
.BR JS8MAP_HOST ,
.BR JS8MAP_PORT ,
.BR JS8MAP_JS8_HOST ,
.BR JS8MAP_JS8_PORT ,
.BR JS8MAP_POLL_SECONDS ,
.BR JS8MAP_TTL_MINUTES ,
.BR JS8MAP_MAX_MESSAGES ,
.BR JS8MAP_OPEN ,
.BR JS8MAP_RECORD ,
.BR JS8MAP_TRANSMIT ,
.BR JS8MAP_DATA_DIR ,
.BR JS8MAP_KEEP_DAYS .
Command-line options override environment variables, which override the
configuration files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run headless on a Raspberry Pi and view it from other devices:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mkdir \-p ~/.config/js8call\-map
echo \(aq{ "webHost": "0.0.0.0" }\(aq > ~/.config/js8call\-map/config.json
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now js8call\-map
sudo loginctl enable\-linger $USER
.EE
.RE
.PP
Record a session for testing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
js8call\-map \-\-record session.jsonl
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR js8call (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/MRC757/JS8CALL\-Map
